			"Message": "refactor(Vine): Standardize code and acronym formatting in README\n\nUpdate the README.md to consistently wrap technical terms and acronyms (TCP, IPC, WASM, gRPC, Mountain, Cocoon, Grove) in backticks for proper Markdown syntax highlighting.\n\nThis change affects the core principles list, feature summary, and implementation details sections. The updates clarify the distinction between the protocol definition (Vine) and the transport implementations, ensuring accurate documentation of the gRPC contract layer.\n\nNo functional changes to the protocol definition; strictly documentation formatting.",
			"SHA": "9ce8c55b3ac971134b2cfdbb47e9d2d9691fa549"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-13T21:13:05Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				5,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Vine): Correct License URL to point to Vine repository\n\nUpdate the License badge and footer link in README.md to reference the actual location of the CC0 LICENSE file within the Vine repository, replacing the incorrect pointer to the parent Land repository.\n\nThis ensures compliance with the project's open-source documentation standards and prevents broken links for developers reviewing the protocol definition layer.",
			"SHA": "faacc3fbcd86c0080459b17ccbe4ac262437ecdc"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-03T06:21:27Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⣿⠀⠀⠀",
				5,
				2
			],
			"Message": "chore(Vine): Remove obsolete proto file references in README\n\nThe README.md listed local `Source/` directories and specific proto paths as current implementation locations. However, Vine serves strictly as the documentation surface for the gRPC contract, while the actual `.proto` definitions and Rust implementations reside in Mountain and Grove repositories.\n\nRemove the misleading `Proto/Spine.proto` and `Source/` path references that imply local existence. Update the description to direct readers to the \"Spine Contract\" documentation for the current specification, ensuring alignment with the project's architecture where the contract is defined externally but documented here.\n\nThis cleanup prevents developer confusion regarding the location of protocol definitions and maintains the README's role as a high-level documentation hub.",
			"SHA": "c5dacffe76fc4e58cb66ef0236792c9b2393ad57"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T15:58:48Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				5,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Vine): Restructure CHANGELOG for clarity and accuracy\n\nRefactor the CHANGELOG entry structure to better communicate Vine's evolution:\n- Add introductory paragraph explaining Vine is the gRPC contract and where `Vine.proto` actually lives (in Mountain's tree)\n- Rename v2.1 from \"Q2 2026\" to \"Full Workbench Lift (April 2026)\" and convert from Changed to Added/Changed format with commit references\n- Simplify v2.0 from detailed RPC listings to \"Editor Launch\" with note about protocol stability through the window\n- Consolidate v1.2 and v1.1 into a single \"Pre-Documentation Scaffold\" section noting Vine existed as a placeholder\n- Add new v0.0 section documenting the original 2025 repository creation\n\nThese changes provide a more accurate historical record while removing verbose RPC listings better suited for protocol reference docs.",
			"SHA": "e2dc32a183e523e2d393553319db40a3b8aebad3"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-21T18:32:41Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⣿⠀⠀⠀",
				5,
				2
			],
			"Message": "docs(Vine): Standardize em dashes to regular dashes in documentation\n\nReplace em dash characters (—) with regular dashes (-) throughout CHANGELOG.md and Documentation/GitHub/DeepDive.md for consistent typography and improved compatibility with various rendering systems.\n\nThis change affects section headers, release dates, and descriptive text across both documentation files, maintaining visual consistency with the project's documentation style guidelines.",
